# CHANGES IN UNRELEASED (pico):

        The pico branch is upstream havoc at commit 73e3467 (version
        0.7.0-git) with five patches for handhelds with a QVGA-class
        panel and about 64 MiB of RAM. There is no pico release or tag
        yet. Status says what is recorded about where they ran.

##        On-screen keyboard:

        * Havoc binds zwp_text_input_manager_v3 when the compositor
          offers it. On keyboard focus it enables a text input with
          content type terminal and the cursor cell as the cursor
          rectangle, and disables it when the focus leaves, so a
          compositor that shows an on-screen keyboard for text fields
          shows one for the terminal. Enabling happens once per focus.
          Keys still arrive through wl_keyboard; the text events are
          ignored.

##        Damage:

        * A redraw damages only the cells that changed, found from a
          key per cell (symbol, width and the two colours after cursor,
          selection and inverse are applied), not from libtsm's ages.
          Each buffer remembers what it was painted with, so only
          changed cells are painted. One rectangle per run of changed
          rows, a bounding box above eight runs, the whole surface when
          three quarters of the cells changed. A frame with no change
          is not committed.

        * At opacity 255 the window sets its opaque region to the whole
          surface and uses XRGB8888 buffers.

        * A narrow character written over half of a wide one clears the
          other half, and a wide cell in the last column is clipped.

        * HAVOC_FULL_REDRAW in the environment paints and damages
          everything on every redraw, as a reference for tests.

##        Emoji:

        * A code point at or above U+2000 that is in a wvkbd emoji pack
          (emoji-10.pack, emoji-12.pack, emoji-16.pack, emoji-24.pack)
          is drawn as that picture, in colour, two cells wide. The pack
          is the largest that fits two cells by one, or the next smaller
          one when that file is missing or refused. Without a pack the
          code point is drawn from the font as before.

        * A pack is untrusted input: every offset, length and count is
          checked before use, and a pack that fails is not used. The
          directory is -E DIR, else HAVOC_EMOJI_DIR, else the Makefile's
          EMOJI_DIR (/usr/share/wvkbd/emoji).

        * libtsm has a callback, tsm_screen_set_picture_cb(), that gives
          two cells to every code point a pack has. A picture is never
          cut at the right margin.

##        Bitmap fonts:

        * [font] pixel=yes draws the text from the X11 misc-fixed bitmap
          fonts, compiled in: 5x8, 6x10, 6x12, 6x13, 7x13, 7x14, 9x18
          and 10x20, 122 KB together. Each cell is the foreground or
          the background colour, nothing blended. pixel=yes picks the
          largest font not higher than [font] size, and from size 40 the
          10x20 font in whole multiples, so the zoom keys work.
          pixel=<name>, such as pixel=6x13, picks one font. No outline
          font is opened in this mode. The default is the outline font,
          with the same pixels as before.

        * A code point a font lacks is drawn as the font's empty box.
          Bold, underline and blink are not drawn, as in havoc.

##        C8 buffers:

        * [window] c8=yes draws 8-bit indexed (C8) buffers, a quarter of
          the bytes of XRGB8888, and sends the colours with the
          picowl-palette-v1 protocol. It applies only while the
          compositor offers that protocol and the C8 shm format, reports
          the window as exclusive on its output, opacity is 255 and a
          bitmap font is in use. Otherwise, and after any change of
          these, havoc draws XRGB8888 and repaints the whole window.

        * The palette has the xterm 6x6x6 cube at 16 to 231 and 40 slots
          for the other colours the cells use. A colour with no slot
          left is drawn as the nearest cube colour until the next
          redraw, which starts the table over. Emoji are drawn in the
          nearest colours without taking slots.

##        Build:

        * PIXFONT_OBJ=pixfont-none.o builds without the bitmap font
          data. PICOWL_PALETTE_XML names the picowl-palette-v1.xml file
          (it comes with picowl, not with this tree); without it havoc
          has no C8 code. EMOJI_DIR sets the default pack directory.

##        Status:

        * The pico branch has no test suite, and this repository records
          no test results or device runs for these patches.

        * havoc.cfg does not list the keys [window] c8 and [font] pixel
          yet.

        * Not shown: no pictures of the bitmap fonts, the emoji or a C8
          window have been made yet. They are needed before a release.

        * Sixel and a subset of the kitty graphics protocol, with the
          make variables HAVOC_SIXEL, HAVOC_KITTY and HAVOC_PNG, the
          [graphics] keys and a test suite, are in pull request 1
          (branch graphics) and not on pico. Its NEWS entry goes with
          that pull request.

##        Compatibility:

        * New config keys: [window] c8, [font] pixel. New option: -E.
          New environment variables: HAVOC_EMOJI_DIR,
          HAVOC_FULL_REDRAW. New make variables: EMOJI_DIR, PIXFONT_OBJ,
          PICOWL_PALETTE_XML. With none of them set, havoc behaves as
          upstream except for the damage and the opaque region, and
          code points that a pack in the default directory has.
